# Independent second encoding of the AI-Intent Mandates (ROADMAP 3.2), written from the natural-language
# Mandate texts and risk parameters only, not from agents/constraint_spec.py. Formalism: SHACL-SPARQL over
# the oracle's own RDF rendering of an agent response (evaluation/oracle_agreement.py). Each shape names
# the rule id it encodes; a validation result is a violation of that rule. Shapes apply only when the
# typed field they read is present, because the gate's prose fallback has no counterpart here.
@prefix sh:  <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix ex:  <https://github.com/InformationServiceSystems/ai-intent/oracle#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

ex: sh:declare [ sh:prefix "ex" ; sh:namespace "https://github.com/InformationServiceSystems/ai-intent/oracle#"^^xsd:anyURI ] .
